{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310628,"nonce":"my5XVim/iiy6G30TvU/NFy8/XVc=","title":"`cast(x:SrcIface, TgtIface)` where TgtIface has more methods than SrcIface (e.g. `cast(model:Module, CausalLanguageModel)`) reinterpreted ...","message":"PARTIAL FIX in commit b9f407d. Iface→Iface cast used to be a bare `build_cast` (pass-through). When `TgtIface extends SrcIface`, the source fat pointer's vtable only has SrcIface's method slots. Any virtual call on a TgtIface-only method (e.g. `model.resetCache()` where model was cast Module→CausalLanguageModel) reads past the allocated slots and lands on garbage → SIGSEGV on the indirect call.\n\nInfrastructure landed:\n- Runtime `IFACE_VTABLE_REGISTRY: (class_tid, iface_tid) → Vec\u003cclosure_ptr\u003e`, populated via `haxe_iface_vtable_set_slot`, read by `haxe_iface_fat_ptr_build(obj_ptr, target_iface_tid)`. The build helper extracts class_tid from the object header, looks up the matching vtable, mallocs a new fat pointer, fills in obj + closures.\n- Compiler `__vtable_init__` registers each (class_sym, iface_sym, slot, closure) entry via the new runtime call. Looks up the closure in both `function_map` and `external_function_map`.\n- Cast handler routes Interface→Interface through the rebuild helper when target's method count exceeds source's; otherwise keeps the pass-through.\n\n**Persistence half landed in commit c7a170d.** `BladeCachedMaps` now carries `interface_vtables` as `(class_qname, iface_qname, method_qnames)` triples; both build and restore handle them. After this commit the user-context's `interface_vtables` map sees all 18 (class, iface) pairs for llama-chat including `(LlamaModel, CausalLanguageModel)` with its 4 methods, and the MIR emit in `__vtable_init__` produces the right `haxe_iface_vtable_set_slot` calls. Verified at compile time via `[vtbl-emit]` diagnostics.\n\n**Startup gap closed in commit a8cef3c.** Two issues uncovered + fixed:\n\n1. `run_startup_hooks_{interpreter,native}` only ran the FIRST `__vtable_init__` per module via `find`. After import merging, multiple `__vtable_init__` functions live in the user module with distinct IrFunctionIds — only the entry file's ran. Switched to `filter`+iterate so every per-file init runs. Native path skips inits whose JIT compilation failed (no `function_pointers` entry) so a trap-stub doesn't SIGILL the program at startup; missing registrations are recoverable, SIGILL is not.\n\n2. The `__vtable_init__` emission for iface vtables fell back to `external_function_map` when the method wasn't locally compiled — that fed `build_function_ref` a renumbered import id Cranelift couldn't resolve at codegen, trap-stubbing the entire init. Restricted to `function_map` only; imported methods register their slot from their OWN file's `__vtable_init__`, which the multi-init runner above now actually invokes.\n\nTogether these mean a (LlamaModel, CausalLanguageModel) entry from nue.arch, persisted into BLADE cache (c7a170d), and replayed into the user-context's `interface_vtables`, now lands in the runtime registry at startup. `haxe_iface_fat_ptr_build` called from an iface-to-iface cast (b9f407d) finds the matching vtable.\n\n**Remaining blocker for llama-chat is a separate pre-existing trap-stub cascade.** Running llama-chat at HEAD shows W0020 cascades on `nue.arch.LlamaArch.build`, `nue.arch.BertArch.build`, `nue.loader.GGUFTokenizer.build` etc. with \"Called function IrFunctionId(280006) not found in module\" — these aren't `__vtable_init__` failures, they're user-code trap-stubs from cross-module function ref resolution failures. The iface infrastructure here is correct; the next investigation should look at why cross-file CallDirect targets get IrFunctionIds the user-module's Cranelift backend can't see.\n\nDiagnostic: `RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1` lists all `__vtable_init__` fn-ptrs and trap-stubs. Compare the `IrFunctionId` cited in W0020 against the IDs in the dump — if the cited ID is missing from the dump entirely, the cross-module merge is dropping it; if it's there but in a different module's range, the renumbering isn't propagating to the caller's references.\n\nRelated: [[bugs-blade-property-orphan]] (similar cross-context replay issue, fixed); [[bugs-iface-method-return-dynamic]] (iface return-type cross-context, fixed).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_iface_to_iface_cast_pass_through` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}